CVA6ConfigDcacheType = WT_CLN Signal Flow Tree
==============================================

1. CONFIGURATION PHASE (cv32a6_imac_sv32_config_pkg.sv)
   └── localparam config_pkg::cache_type_t CVA6ConfigDcacheType = config_pkg::WT_CLN;
       └── cva6_cfg.'{ DCacheType: CVA6ConfigDcacheType }

2. BUILD/DERIVATION PHASE (build_config_pkg.sv)
   └── CVA6Cfg.DCacheType = config_pkg::WT_CLN
       └── cfg.DCacheType = CVA6Cfg.DCacheType;

3. MODULE INSTANTIATION PHASE
   └── std_cache_subsystem (core/cache_subsystem/std_cache_subsystem.sv)
       └── Cache type selection via generate blocks:
           ├── if (CVA6Cfg.DCacheType == config_pkg::WT_CLN) → Use WT_CLN cache
           ├── if (CVA6Cfg.DCacheType == config_pkg::WB) → Use WB cache  
           └── if (CVA6Cfg.DCacheType == config_pkg::WT) → Use WT cache

4. WT_CLN SPECIFIC INSTANTIATION
   └── wt_cln_dcache_ctrler (core/cache_subsystem/wt_cln_dcache_ctrl.sv)
       ├── Cache controller for write-through clean policy
       ├── wt_cln_dcache_mem (core/cache_subsystem/wt_cln_dcache_mem.sv)
       │   └── Memory array with clean/dirty state tracking
       └── wt_cln_axi_adapter (core/cache_subsystem/wt_cln_axi_adapter.sv)
           └── AXI interface adapter for write-through operations

5. FUNCTIONAL IMPACT
   └── Write-Through Clean Behavior:
       ├── All writes immediately propagate to memory
       ├── Cache lines maintain clean state (no dirty bits needed)
       ├── Simplified coherency (no writeback required)
       ├── Read hits serve directly from cache
       └── Write hits update cache and memory simultaneously

6. INTERFACE CONNECTIONS
   └── Cache controller interfaces:
       ├── CPU-side: req_port_i/resp_port_o
       ├── Memory-side: axi_req_o/axi_resp_i  
       └── Bypass logic for uncacheable addresses

KEY RELATIONSHIPS:
- DCacheType = WT_CLN selects write-through clean cache architecture
- Determines cache coherency policy and memory update behavior
- Affects power consumption (more memory writes) vs. complexity tradeoffs
- Eliminates need for dirty bit tracking and writeback logic